  "problem": "Find the solutions **in radians** to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x=7$ for $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi .$ Round your answers to **one decimal place**.\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$\n{{field-1}} and $x=$\n{{field-2}}.",
  "worked_solution": "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(7)=1.428\\,899\u2026\u22481.4\n$$\n\nSince $1.4$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=1.4.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=-\\pi +{x}_{1}=-\\pi +1.428\\,899\u2026\u2248-1.7.\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order and rounded to one decimal place, the solutions are $x=-1.7$ and $x=1.4.$",
